infographic compare-quadrant-quarter-simple-card
data
  title Two questions, four directive choices
  desc May a cache STORE it? × Is it per-user or shared-safe? — each cell names the Cache-Control that fits.
  compares
    - label Sensitive / per-user → private, no-store
      desc Bank balance, password-reset, signed-in dashboard. no-store keeps it off disk and out of bfcache; private excludes the CDN. Never shared, never stored.
    - label Personalized but storable → private, max-age=0
      desc Per-user but cacheable in the browser only. private keeps it off the shared CDN; revalidate before reuse. Pair with Vary: Cookie as belt-and-suspenders.
    - label Shared HTML that changes → no-cache (max-age=0, must-revalidate)
      desc Public document that must always pick up new asset URLs. Stored, but revalidated every time so it is never served stale.
    - label Content-hashed asset → public, max-age=31536000, immutable
      desc app.4f3a9c.js never changes under that URL, so cache it for a year and skip revalidation entirely. Hash the assets, never the HTML.
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #6366f1 #14b8a6
